  "text": "In a conventional example, the normal supply passes through distribution and an uninterruptible power supply, or UPS, before reaching equipment. If the incoming source fails, stored energy can bridge the transition while a backup generator starts. The animation illustrates that sequence. Actual designs differ, and backup operation depends on capacity, fuel, controls, and maintenance. A generator alone doesn't mean there can be no interruption at the equipment.",
